1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
<font color="#FF8040">{\an8}Downloaded From MoviesMod.Org</font>

2
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:08,008
[upbeat music playing]

3
00:00:12,012 --> 00:00:12,971
[door opens]

4
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:15,473
Oh, hey.

5
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:17,976
Hi.

6
00:00:19,477 --> 00:00:20,979
[Alex] Going for a run?

7
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:22,689
Yeah. You?

8
00:00:22,772 --> 00:00:24,858
I'm just heading out for practice.

9
00:00:24,941 --> 00:00:26,860
The tryouts for Blake's dad
are in a couple weeks,

10
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:28,361
and I really want that sponsorship.

11
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:31,322
-You'll do great.
-I wanted to talk to you.

12
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:33,616
Now that I passed my driver's test--

13
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:35,827
All right, no need to rub it in.

14
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:38,663
I don't know why you're so nervous.
You'll be fine.

15
00:00:39,456 --> 00:00:40,540
Okay, thanks.

16
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:43,626
I was thinking.
I want us to go on a real date.

17
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,587
Yeah, okay. I guess.

18
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:48,423
But we'll have to go somewhere
where no one will see us.

19
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:51,885
The movies? We could go to Lockwood.
The Mirror Ball's showing horror classics.

20
00:00:51,968 --> 00:00:53,219
Yeah, sounds good.

21
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:55,555
Okay, so I'll say I'm going to a party
with the rodeo guys.

22
00:00:55,638 --> 00:00:58,475
And I'll say that I'm going to Grace's.

23
00:01:03,229 --> 00:01:04,064
Hey.

24
00:01:04,647 --> 00:01:05,648
-Hey.
-Hey.

25
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,318
What are you guys doin'?

26
00:01:09,486 --> 00:01:11,571
-Nothing.
-I'm just going to practice.

27
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:19,120
Um… so the parallel parking is
at the end of the road test?

28
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:22,373
Yes, after all of the… driving.

29
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:26,252
-Got it.
-[Alex] Yeah.

30
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:29,172
-You're gonna ace it.
-Hope so.

31
00:01:29,255 --> 00:01:30,131
[Alex chuckles]

32
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:33,218
Okay, well, guess I'll see you guys later.

33
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:34,302
See ya.

34
00:01:53,071 --> 00:01:53,988
Beautiful out.

35
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:03,540
[Will] Okay, Dad,
what are we doing out here?

36
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:05,375
See this?

37
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:07,877
It's loam soil.

38
00:02:08,753 --> 00:02:10,713
Is that a good thing?

39
00:02:11,297 --> 00:02:13,341
Yeah, if you want to grow grapes.

40
00:02:13,424 --> 00:02:14,384
Grapes?

41
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:17,971
-What's going on?
-Okay.

42
00:02:18,054 --> 00:02:23,268
So apparently your dad's great-grandfather
made wine during Prohibition.

43
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:26,354
And we always knew there'd be grapes
somewhere, but we just didn't know where.

44
00:02:26,437 --> 00:02:28,731
Until I found this vine. Look.

45
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:30,817
When I was out looking for Murphy.

46
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:33,611
This thing has survived
out here all that time.

47
00:02:33,695 --> 00:02:37,198
I mean, this is the answer
to our financial problems, Will.

48
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:41,327
I thought the guest ranch
was our answer, Dad.

49
00:02:41,911 --> 00:02:43,746
The guest ranch
was supposed to be me and you,

50
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:45,331
some yurts, and horseback riding.

51
00:02:45,915 --> 00:02:49,085
And I blinked,
and there was a lodge in our front yard.

52
00:02:49,169 --> 00:02:52,172
And… and Richard just taking
the whole thing over.

53
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:55,091
So I'll talk to him.
We'll scale it back to what it was.

54
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:56,259
It's too late, Will.

55
00:02:57,302 --> 00:02:59,304
-I'm ending it.
-[Will] You can't do that.

56
00:02:59,387 --> 00:03:02,056
We paid for the permits.
We've run the utility lines.

57
00:03:02,557 --> 00:03:05,476
-There's a contract.
-I'm gonna go talk to Richard about that.

58
00:03:06,978 --> 00:03:08,980
So you're just going to start a winery?

59
00:03:10,106 --> 00:03:14,402
Do you have any idea how hard that is?
How long it takes to turn a profit?

60
00:03:14,485 --> 00:03:15,945
Yeah, we do.

61
00:03:17,238 --> 00:03:19,991
Which is why we're gonna lease
the land to Little Cap Winery.

62
00:03:20,783 --> 00:03:23,453
The income's immediate, and we can
start to pay back our investors.

63
00:03:28,082 --> 00:03:30,418
So… that's it?

64
00:03:30,501 --> 00:03:32,629
Look, I know it's a pivot,

65
00:03:33,922 --> 00:03:35,256
but this is going to be better.

66
00:03:35,882 --> 00:03:36,883
For all of us.

67
00:03:39,385 --> 00:03:41,387
[somber music playing]

68
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:53,316
So, have you thought
more about Día de los Muertos?

69
00:03:53,399 --> 00:03:55,360
I know you didn't want
to do anything last year,

70
00:03:55,443 --> 00:03:58,905
but I was thinking
maybe we could get together tomorrow

71
00:03:58,988 --> 00:04:00,782
before I fly back to New York?

72
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:03,076
You're going back to New York?

73
00:04:03,576 --> 00:04:06,663
Yeah, I have some meetings
about the ranch.

74
00:04:07,205 --> 00:04:09,457
Is everything going okay now
with the ranch?

75
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:10,833
After the barn and everything?

76
00:04:12,085 --> 00:04:14,587
You know these things aren't
without their hiccups along the way,

77
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:16,714
but it'll all work out.

78
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:18,716
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

79
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,677
Nothing for you to worry about, all right?

80
00:04:21,886 --> 00:04:22,720
All right.

81
00:04:24,305 --> 00:04:26,599
So… tomorrow?

82
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:30,520
I don't know.

83
00:04:31,145 --> 00:04:33,356
Up to you. We can always do it next year.

84
00:04:34,399 --> 00:04:35,233
Sure.

85
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:45,368
I feel bad about Will.

86
00:04:45,451 --> 00:04:46,744
[horse whinnies]

87
00:04:46,828 --> 00:04:48,037
He worked so hard.

88
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:50,873
I'll give it a minute
and then go talk to him.

89
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:53,334
I don't think Richard's
gonna take it much better.

90
00:04:53,418 --> 00:04:55,336
Well, that one's not my problem.

91
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,171
Yeah, but, um…

92
00:04:59,173 --> 00:05:01,259
he wanted to tell you this himself.

93
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:02,218
Oh boy. What?

94
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,679
He's in over his head financially.

95
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:07,390
He used his own money for this.

96
00:05:07,473 --> 00:05:09,100
He said he had investors.

97
00:05:10,184 --> 00:05:11,311
Why would he do that?

98
00:05:12,687 --> 00:05:14,480
'Cause Jackie's
the only family he's got left.

99
00:05:18,526 --> 00:05:20,528
[upbeat music playing]

100
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:30,663
Okay, that's ten volunteers for
the community garden clean up next week.

101
00:05:31,622 --> 00:05:34,125
Then I think that's it for today.

102
00:05:34,208 --> 00:05:38,129
Oh, Principal Whitmore asked us
to hang these posters up in school.

103
00:05:38,212 --> 00:05:42,967
So maybe everyone can take a few posters
and hang them up on your way out.

104
00:05:43,843 --> 00:05:47,555
I've seen these around town.
The Silver Falls Sparkle?

105
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:48,765
Yeah, it's pretty fun.

106
00:05:48,848 --> 00:05:50,892
The whole town's
decorated in these twinkly lights.

107
00:05:50,975 --> 00:05:54,354
There's food trucks and games and music.
Hot chocolate.

108
00:05:54,437 --> 00:05:55,855
The church does a charity raffle.

109
00:05:55,938 --> 00:05:58,566
Yeah, and there's an awards ceremony
for people that have done, like,

110
00:05:58,649 --> 00:06:01,694
cool or special things
to contribute to the town in some way.

111
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:03,946
It's the most Silver Falls thing ever.

112
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,239
[Erin and Grace chuckle]

113
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:06,908
Great. What can we do to help?

114
00:06:06,991 --> 00:06:09,327
Nothing. There's a town committee
that handles everything.

115
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:14,832
Okay, that's it. See you guys next week,
and happy Halloween.

116
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:16,334
-[Grace] Yeah.
-[Skylar] Ooh.

117
00:06:16,834 --> 00:06:17,877
Thanks, Erin.

118
00:06:19,212 --> 00:06:20,838
[Grace] So, I was thinking about tonight.

119
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:23,466
The house on Rogers Street
always goes all out as a haunted house.

120
00:06:23,549 --> 00:06:26,552
And I've never been 'cause my parents.
Plus, it does look really scary.

121
00:06:26,636 --> 00:06:29,222
But I was thinking if we go together,
it could be kind of fun.

122
00:06:30,139 --> 00:06:32,558
Actually, Alex and I are going on a date.

123
00:06:33,267 --> 00:06:34,143
Oh.

124
00:06:34,727 --> 00:06:37,522
So I was hoping
I could say I was with you.

125
00:06:38,189 --> 00:06:42,110
Uh, sure. Yeah. I love being
a cover story for a secret rendezvous.

126
00:06:43,194 --> 00:06:45,822
-Thanks.
-Where are you guys going?

127
00:06:45,905 --> 00:06:48,491
Okay. So what are we doing
for Halloween tonight?

128
00:06:48,574 --> 00:06:49,742
Uh, nothing.

129
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:52,829
Nothing. I gotta study
for the math test next week.

130
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:55,039
Got a D on the last one
and my dad hit the roof.

131
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:58,042
So, uh, yeah, Jackie's gonna come over
and help me study.

132
00:06:58,126 --> 00:06:58,960
Right, Jackie?

133
00:06:59,043 --> 00:07:00,044
Oh, right.

134
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:02,380
I think I want to have
a Halloween party tonight.

135
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:06,717
Do you really feel up to throwing a party
after the whole Zach and Nathan thing?

136
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:09,554
Honestly, I'm hoping
it'll make me feel better.

137
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:12,515
Right. Well, Halloween's in six hours.

138
00:07:12,598 --> 00:07:16,227
And six hours isn't enough time
to put together a whole party.

139
00:07:16,727 --> 00:07:20,523
It doesn't have to be fancy.
There's this space above Monty's.

140
00:07:20,606 --> 00:07:23,151
It's kinda creepy. We could do it there.

141
00:07:23,234 --> 00:07:26,612
Grace, you can spread the word around
the whole school before last period.

142
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:29,198
Uh, yeah, I guess.

143
00:07:30,408 --> 00:07:33,578
But what about food, decorations, drinks?

144
00:07:33,661 --> 00:07:35,955
Jackie, come on.

145
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:37,415
I need this.

146
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:39,041
After Nathan.

147
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:42,044
Okay.

148
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:43,171
-Yay! [laughs]
-I'll help.

149
00:07:43,254 --> 00:07:44,088
[Grace squeals]

150
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:46,257
Alex, wanna come to our Halloween party?

151
00:07:48,634 --> 00:07:50,636
-Tonight?
-[Skylar] Yeah, it's Halloween.

152
00:07:51,554 --> 00:07:54,891
We can't. We're on little-kid duty
for trick-or-treating. Remember?

153
00:07:54,974 --> 00:07:57,602
I thought you just said
you were studying with Grace?

154
00:07:58,102 --> 00:07:59,103
Uh…

155
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:00,771
[spluttering]

156
00:08:00,855 --> 00:08:04,192
Yeah, that's after.

157
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:06,486
So come to the party instead.

158
00:08:13,534 --> 00:08:16,078
Okay, sure. Yeah, see you there.

159
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:18,164
-Happy Halloween!
-[Skylar chuckles]

160
00:08:18,247 --> 00:08:20,208
-I'll see y'all tonight, okay?
-Okay.

161
00:08:22,835 --> 00:08:26,297
-What was that about?
-Oh, Skylar's having a Halloween party.

162
00:08:27,381 --> 00:08:29,091
Guess I'm not invited, huh?

163
00:08:29,634 --> 00:08:31,260
I'll stay home with you.

164
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:32,762
You're still not talking to Erin?

165
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:35,056
I don't think she's talking to me.

166
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,308
Scary movie night it is.

167
00:08:38,059 --> 00:08:40,436
[overlapping chatter]

168
00:08:45,316 --> 00:08:48,611
Okay, everybody! Listen up! Listen up.

169
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:54,534
I was in high school once.

170
00:08:55,159 --> 00:08:58,704
So I understand
the pressures to partake in drugs

171
00:08:58,788 --> 00:08:59,705
and alcohol.

172
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:03,543
But as student athletes, we need
to hold ourselves to higher standards.

173
00:09:04,043 --> 00:09:06,546
And sadly, some of you are not doing that.

174
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:15,471
The following players
had positive drug tests

175
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:18,558
and will be suspended from the team
until further notice.

176
00:09:18,641 --> 00:09:19,559
[player] Seriously?

177
00:09:19,642 --> 00:09:23,354
Carter Reeves, Sean Stanley,
and Dylan Newsome.

178
00:09:24,772 --> 00:09:25,606
Isaac.

179
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:30,236
-You're our new quarterback.
-[player 2] No, what?!

180
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:32,280
[overlapping chatter]

181
00:09:41,247 --> 00:09:43,124
Dylan, hey, wait up.

182
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:44,250
What do you want?

183
00:09:45,793 --> 00:09:47,587
-Are you okay?
-No, I'm not.

184
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:50,047
Because of you, I'm benched.
No way we'll make playoffs.

185
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:52,633
Wait. It's not my fault
you failed your drug test.

186
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:54,176
But you got exactly what you wanted.

187
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,386
Your cousin is quarterback,

188
00:09:55,469 --> 00:09:57,513
and you don't have to watch me
outshine you.

189
00:09:57,597 --> 00:10:00,725
Are you serious?
I've been trying to help you.

190
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:02,602
Help? [scoffs]

191
00:10:03,394 --> 00:10:05,062
You pushed me so hard,
I almost got injured.

192
00:10:05,146 --> 00:10:07,732
I pushed you so that you'd play better,
so that we'd win.

193
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:10,484
-That's what a good coach does.
-No, you know what you should've done?

194
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:13,195
Taken the test for me.

195
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:16,240
But you didn't because you've been on
a mission to sabotage me since day one.

196
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:17,283
Is that what you think?

197
00:10:18,492 --> 00:10:22,079
We just got a clean slate.
Why would I risk that after everything?

198
00:10:22,163 --> 00:10:23,664
No one would've found out.

199
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:29,003
[scoffs] It's always
someone else's fault, isn't it?

200
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:31,672
And sabotage?

201
00:10:32,381 --> 00:10:34,759
You don't need me for that.
Doing a great job on your own.

202
00:10:38,929 --> 00:10:40,598
Okay. [clears throat]

203
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:44,852
Do you accelerate or decelerate
when exiting a freeway ramp?

204
00:10:44,935 --> 00:10:46,354
-Decelerate.
-Perfect.

205
00:10:47,188 --> 00:10:50,441
What do you do if your view
is blocked at a crosswalk?

206
00:10:50,524 --> 00:10:55,321
Move forward carefully and look both ways
before slowly entering the intersection.

207
00:10:55,404 --> 00:10:56,405
[Alex] Perfect.

208
00:10:57,698 --> 00:11:01,035
Hey. I got our tickets
for the movie tonight.

209
00:11:01,702 --> 00:11:02,536
Great.

210
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:06,165
So we'll just have to stop by
Skylar's party first.

211
00:11:06,248 --> 00:11:07,541
I'll be there early to set up.

212
00:11:07,625 --> 00:11:10,127
Then we'll need to leave separately
so that no one will suspect--

213
00:11:10,211 --> 00:11:11,212
-Right.

214
00:11:13,130 --> 00:11:17,218
You know, maybe one of these days
we can actually go to a party together.

215
00:11:17,301 --> 00:11:18,886
Yeah, of course.

216
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:23,891
I just think
that with everything going on,

217
00:11:23,974 --> 00:11:26,936
now's not the best time to tell anyone.
Don't you?

218
00:11:27,353 --> 00:11:28,729
Yeah, sure.

219
00:11:33,526 --> 00:11:34,402
No.

220
00:11:37,113 --> 00:11:38,030
What is it?

221
00:11:40,908 --> 00:11:41,742
I…

222
00:11:43,619 --> 00:11:45,287
I just… it's almost gone.

223
00:11:46,455 --> 00:11:48,082
Can't you just get another bottle?

224
00:11:48,582 --> 00:11:50,918
No. And that's not the point.

225
00:11:54,672 --> 00:11:56,048
It was my mom's.

226
00:11:56,924 --> 00:11:58,008
Oh.

227
00:12:00,010 --> 00:12:00,886
I'm sorry. I--

228
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:03,556
It's okay. It's just perfume.

229
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:07,560
It's fine. I'll be fine.

230
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:10,062
Um…

231
00:12:10,896 --> 00:12:12,314
But I… I better go.

232
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:15,025
Okay. You're gonna do great.

233
00:12:15,693 --> 00:12:16,610
Thanks.

234
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:22,616
[sighs]

235
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:25,661
How the hell did Garcia
even make second string?

236
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:27,955
Dude, he overthrows me every time.

237
00:12:28,038 --> 00:12:28,873
[Jay] Yo, Cole.

238
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:32,668
I know he's your cousin and all,

239
00:12:32,752 --> 00:12:34,420
but he can't hit a target
to save his life.

240
00:12:34,503 --> 00:12:37,798
Right. I forgot you guys
were perfect on your first day.

241
00:12:40,843 --> 00:12:42,052
Give him a break.

242
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:45,639
Give him a break.

243
00:12:46,432 --> 00:12:47,475
Ready to begin?

244
00:12:48,434 --> 00:12:49,268
Ready.

245
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:54,899
The orange cones represent other vehicles
for you to maneuver around.

246
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:58,569
Be very mindful of those
as you reverse out of the parking space.

247
00:12:58,652 --> 00:12:59,737
Got it.

248
00:13:00,321 --> 00:13:04,700
All right, back out past the last cone,
then exit the parking lot that way.

249
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:13,250
Sorry, these brakes are
a little more sensitive than I'm used to.

250
00:13:22,968 --> 00:13:24,970
Hey! Put the vehicle in park.

251
00:13:25,054 --> 00:13:26,347
