Okay, tomorrow will be better.

505
00:25:55,053 --> 00:25:56,596
Tomorrow is worse.

506
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:58,306
Tomorrow is the Day of the…

507
00:26:02,477 --> 00:26:03,895
-Oh no, you don't.
-Wait.

508
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:06,565
Hey, hey, where are you going?

509
00:26:06,648 --> 00:26:09,943
-To rip that outfit off that stupid--
-Whoa. What outfit?

510
00:26:10,443 --> 00:26:12,445
That's La Calavera Catrina.

511
00:26:13,029 --> 00:26:16,283
And I bet that she has no idea
who that is or what that even means.

512
00:26:17,576 --> 00:26:20,495
-So?
-So she shouldn't be wearing it.

513
00:26:20,579 --> 00:26:23,164
Okay, okay, hey. Settle down.

514
00:26:24,541 --> 00:26:26,459
Look at me. Look at me.

515
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:29,254
Breathe.

516
00:26:30,463 --> 00:26:31,506
[exhales]

517
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:34,342
You okay?

518
00:26:37,804 --> 00:26:38,638
Fine.

519
00:26:54,195 --> 00:26:57,032
-Are you sure we shouldn't call 911?
-[Kiley] No.

520
00:26:57,115 --> 00:26:59,868
No, she doesn't need a doctor.
She needs to sleep it off.

521
00:27:01,202 --> 00:27:03,413
This happens all the time.
She'll be fine in the morning.

522
00:27:03,913 --> 00:27:05,999
[Alex] I had no idea, Kyles.

523
00:27:07,375 --> 00:27:08,418
Why didn't you tell me?

524
00:27:09,294 --> 00:27:11,421
We haven't really been talking much.

525
00:27:13,798 --> 00:27:16,092
Um… well, you gotta tell someone.

526
00:27:17,218 --> 00:27:19,512
-Like who?
-I don't know. A teacher or something.

527
00:27:19,596 --> 00:27:23,391
If I tell a teacher or a doctor,
they'll call Child Protective Services.

528
00:27:24,684 --> 00:27:25,852
And then what?

529
00:27:26,478 --> 00:27:28,480
-What do you think would happen to me?
-I don't know.

530
00:27:28,563 --> 00:27:30,357
Foster care, Alex.

531
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:33,526
-I'm not doing that.
-Kiley.

532
00:27:35,028 --> 00:27:38,782
Your grandma's the adult.
She should be taking care of you.

533
00:27:38,865 --> 00:27:40,033
Yes, you're right.

534
00:27:41,242 --> 00:27:42,285
She should.

535
00:27:43,995 --> 00:27:45,830
But not everybody gets a perfect family.

536
00:27:47,749 --> 00:27:49,751
[somber music playing]

537
00:27:54,255 --> 00:27:55,548
[Cole] Hey. Hey.

538
00:27:58,760 --> 00:28:00,428
Is this about the driving test?

539
00:28:00,929 --> 00:28:03,932
Because Will failed his first time out.

540
00:28:04,432 --> 00:28:07,602
-So did I. And Danny, he--
-Failed three times.

541
00:28:07,686 --> 00:28:08,520
I know!

542
00:28:10,063 --> 00:28:12,524
Wait, how did you know I didn't pass?

543
00:28:12,607 --> 00:28:15,694
Well, there's no secrets
in the Walter household. So…

544
00:28:19,656 --> 00:28:21,825
If it's not the test, then

545
00:28:23,201 --> 00:28:24,369
what is it?

546
00:28:27,038 --> 00:28:28,498
I know it sounds stupid,

547
00:28:29,332 --> 00:28:30,750
but it's about tomorrow.

548
00:28:32,794 --> 00:28:33,878
Tomorrow?

549
00:28:35,547 --> 00:28:37,257
Día de los Muertos.

550
00:28:38,633 --> 00:28:42,554
It means something, you know?
It's not just a costume.

551
00:28:43,805 --> 00:28:48,977
It's supposed to be a celebration
for those who have died.

552
00:28:50,145 --> 00:28:52,147
And I just… I can't do it.

553
00:28:52,230 --> 00:28:54,816
-Don't beat yourself up.
-What is wrong with me?

554
00:28:55,650 --> 00:28:59,028
-Why can't I celebrate my family?
-There is nothing wrong with you.

555
00:28:59,112 --> 00:29:02,615
And there's still time,
if you want to do it.

556
00:29:06,661 --> 00:29:07,704
Tomorrow

557
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:11,624
is about keeping their memories alive.

558
00:29:12,917 --> 00:29:14,210
But they're fading.

559
00:29:16,087 --> 00:29:20,592
And when I'm in New York
and I'm surrounded by the places we went

560
00:29:20,675 --> 00:29:22,093
or the things we did together,

561
00:29:22,177 --> 00:29:24,220
they feel… they feel closer.

562
00:29:24,846 --> 00:29:26,765
You know, it feels more real.

563
00:29:28,224 --> 00:29:30,643
But they were never here in Silver Falls,

564
00:29:30,727 --> 00:29:33,730
so it's like
there's nothing of them to hold onto.

565
00:29:33,813 --> 00:29:38,902
And the more that I try to fit in here,
the further it feels like I am from them.

566
00:29:39,569 --> 00:29:41,988
I think… I think I'm losing them, Cole.

567
00:29:42,071 --> 00:29:45,867
And I… I'm kinda…
I'm kind losing myself too.

568
00:29:45,950 --> 00:29:48,745
No, you're… you're not losing yourself.

569
00:29:50,747 --> 00:29:51,581
Hey.

570
00:29:52,499 --> 00:29:54,459
You will always be a Howard.

571
00:29:58,421 --> 00:30:00,381
And to me…

572
00:30:03,134 --> 00:30:04,511
you'll always be New York.

573
00:30:09,516 --> 00:30:10,350
Okay?

574
00:30:11,142 --> 00:30:11,976
Hey.

575
00:30:12,644 --> 00:30:13,478
Yeah.

576
00:30:14,479 --> 00:30:15,522
Let's get you home.

577
00:30:16,815 --> 00:30:17,649
Okay.

578
00:30:27,200 --> 00:30:28,201
[Kiley] Thank you.

579
00:30:28,910 --> 00:30:30,036
For coming.

580
00:30:30,119 --> 00:30:31,871
Nah, you can always call me.

581
00:30:36,042 --> 00:30:39,254
Can you not tell anyone… about this?

582
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:40,839
Course not.

583
00:30:50,181 --> 00:30:53,059
So is this why you've been,
like, off lately?

584
00:30:53,142 --> 00:30:54,143
Me?

585
00:30:55,353 --> 00:30:56,271
Alex,

586
00:30:56,354 --> 00:30:59,732
since you came back from rodeo school,
you haven't had room for me.

587
00:30:59,816 --> 00:31:03,194
Yeah, because you've made it pretty clear
you don't want to be around me anymore.

588
00:31:03,278 --> 00:31:05,530
You just seem mad at me all the time.

589
00:31:06,573 --> 00:31:07,699
I'm not mad at you.

590
00:31:07,782 --> 00:31:08,825
Then what is it?

591
00:31:12,996 --> 00:31:14,789
At Will and Haley's wedding…

592
00:31:17,542 --> 00:31:21,254
you said I was practically a dude.

593
00:31:21,337 --> 00:31:22,547
Ah.

594
00:31:23,506 --> 00:31:24,591
Did I?

595
00:31:25,091 --> 00:31:26,092
Mm-hmm.

596
00:31:26,801 --> 00:31:27,802
Ah.

597
00:31:29,429 --> 00:31:31,806
I just meant that you're, like,

598
00:31:32,348 --> 00:31:35,768
really cool and easy to be around.

599
00:31:35,852 --> 00:31:37,854
Come on. Kiley.

600
00:31:41,190 --> 00:31:42,650
I've missed you.

601
00:31:49,032 --> 00:31:50,241
I've missed you too.

602
00:32:02,503 --> 00:32:03,463
Kyles?

603
00:32:06,716 --> 00:32:07,800
Yeah?

604
00:32:09,594 --> 00:32:10,637
We okay?

605
00:32:15,141 --> 00:32:15,975
Sure.

606
00:32:18,269 --> 00:32:19,187
We're okay.

607
00:32:27,570 --> 00:32:30,573
[man on TV] Imagine for one moment
the complexity of the human brain.

608
00:32:30,657 --> 00:32:33,409
The same size, perhaps,
but a million times more efficient.

609
00:32:33,493 --> 00:32:36,371
You are just in time
for part two of our double feature.

610
00:32:38,206 --> 00:32:39,540
[Cole] Think I have a better idea.

611
00:32:42,043 --> 00:32:43,044
Candy poker?

612
00:32:45,421 --> 00:32:46,631
-Who's in?
-I'm in.

613
00:32:46,714 --> 00:32:48,341
-Yep.
-[Cole] Yes.

614
00:32:48,925 --> 00:32:51,427
-[Nathan] All right, who's gonna deal?
-[Danny] I can deal.

615
00:32:51,511 --> 00:32:53,763
[Nathan] All right, Danny,
but you better mix 'em up right.

616
00:32:53,846 --> 00:32:54,889
[Danny] Yeah, I will.

617
00:32:55,390 --> 00:32:56,891
New York? You want to play?

618
00:32:56,975 --> 00:32:59,060
I warn you, we're ruthless.

619
00:33:00,478 --> 00:33:02,146
And take all of your candy?

620
00:33:03,314 --> 00:33:04,357
Are you sure?

621
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:07,318
Oh, she's a hustler.

622
00:33:07,986 --> 00:33:09,904
Okay. Let's see what you got.

623
00:33:11,030 --> 00:33:12,448
Challenge accepted.

624
00:33:16,285 --> 00:33:17,912
Guys, come on. Let's play.

625
00:33:24,877 --> 00:33:27,046
Okay. Here we go.

626
00:33:28,339 --> 00:33:29,424
All right.

627
00:33:40,768 --> 00:33:41,894
[Richard sighs]

628
00:33:42,854 --> 00:33:43,855
[Jackie] It's beautiful.

629
00:33:44,856 --> 00:33:46,858
Do you want to say something or should I?

630
00:33:48,317 --> 00:33:49,360
You go ahead.

631
00:33:52,989 --> 00:33:54,949
To the spirits of those we loved,

632
00:33:55,783 --> 00:33:57,702
welcome on this special day.

633
00:33:59,620 --> 00:34:02,373
We honor and celebrate your lives.

634
00:34:04,083 --> 00:34:07,503
The love we shared with you,
we will carry with us forever.

635
00:34:10,882 --> 00:34:12,925
Feliz Día de los Muertos.

636
00:34:13,009 --> 00:34:14,552
Feliz Día de los Muertos.

637
00:34:16,012 --> 00:34:17,138
And, um,

638
00:34:18,473 --> 00:34:20,058
I wanted to show you something.

639
00:34:20,141 --> 00:34:21,142
What is it?

640
00:34:22,643 --> 00:34:23,936
[woman] Okay, here we go.

641
00:34:25,521 --> 00:34:26,814
[Jackie] Oh my God.

642
00:34:27,315 --> 00:34:29,942
-It's my fifth birthday party.
-[Richard] Mm-hmm.

643
00:34:30,026 --> 00:34:31,903
Happy birthday, mi amor.

644
00:34:33,488 --> 00:34:34,405
Here you go.

645
00:34:35,281 --> 00:34:36,199
Make a wish.

646
00:34:39,243 --> 00:34:41,287
Bravo!

647
00:34:42,288 --> 00:34:43,498
Good job.

648
00:34:44,040 --> 00:34:45,458
Where did you get this?

649
00:34:45,541 --> 00:34:47,418
[Richard] I recorded it
all those years ago.

650
00:34:48,586 --> 00:34:49,921
[woman] Hope it doesn't come true.

651
00:34:50,004 --> 00:34:52,673
I haven't been able
to bring myself to watch it.

652
00:34:53,633 --> 00:34:54,634
Until today.

653
00:34:57,595 --> 00:34:59,347
-Today's the perfect time.
-Yeah.

654
00:35:00,264 --> 00:35:02,225
Well, there's plenty more
where this came from.

655
00:35:02,308 --> 00:35:03,601
-Really?
-[Richard] Mm-hmm.

656
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:06,062
I was hoping we could make a day of it.

657
00:35:06,562 --> 00:35:10,149
If you want to. At least until
I have to leave for the airport.

658
00:35:10,233 --> 00:35:11,317
[sniffles]

659
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:13,611
-I'd love that.
-Good. Come on.

660
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:20,284
[door opens]

661
00:35:35,133 --> 00:35:37,802
-Want me to quiz you?
-I know the plays.

662
00:35:47,270 --> 00:35:49,605
Green right, 23 Z-zap on two.

663
00:35:49,689 --> 00:35:54,235
"Z-zap" tells the receiver to run a zap
motion parallel to the line of scrimmage.

664
00:35:54,318 --> 00:35:55,570
Snap's on the second hut.

665
00:35:57,572 --> 00:35:59,365
Don't know what happened
in practice yesterday.

666
00:35:59,448 --> 00:36:00,992
I've been watching Dylan all season.

667
00:36:01,075 --> 00:36:03,244
Well, you just gotta shake off the nerves.

668
00:36:03,327 --> 00:36:05,538
No, I'm not nervous. It's just that…

669
00:36:07,456 --> 00:36:08,457
You know?

670
00:36:12,253 --> 00:36:13,129
Hey.

671
00:36:13,921 --> 00:36:15,256
First time Coach put me in,

672
00:36:15,756 --> 00:36:17,550
I was so freaked out,
I puked in the huddle.

673
00:36:18,134 --> 00:36:20,261
All over the senior running back's cleats.

674
00:36:20,344 --> 00:36:21,679
-Really?
-Mm-hmm.

675
00:36:21,762 --> 00:36:22,930
-Damn.
-[Cole chuckles]

676
00:36:23,431 --> 00:36:26,475
So, you'll be fine. Just… don't puke.

677
00:36:28,060 --> 00:36:29,562
Don't puke. Got it.

678
00:36:30,062 --> 00:36:30,980
[chuckles]

679
00:36:31,063 --> 00:36:31,898
[scoffs]

680
00:36:34,275 --> 00:36:35,359
A lot to learn, though.

681
00:36:35,443 --> 00:36:37,445
[mellow rock music playing]

682
00:36:43,201 --> 00:36:44,410
[knock on door]

683
00:36:46,078 --> 00:36:47,330
Son, how you doing?

684
00:36:47,413 --> 00:36:48,247
[music fades]

685
00:36:50,917 --> 00:36:53,127
Have you, um, spoken with Richard?

686
00:36:55,004 --> 00:36:56,672
-No.
-I have.

687
00:36:57,965 --> 00:36:59,550
I know you're disappointed.

688
00:36:59,634 --> 00:37:00,676
I know how hard you worked.

689
00:37:00,760 --> 00:37:02,678
I just wanna tell you
how proud I am of you,

690
00:37:02,762 --> 00:37:04,430
despite how this turned out.

691
00:37:05,598 --> 00:37:06,515
[scoffs]

692
00:37:07,350 --> 00:37:08,893
You're still shutting it down.

693
00:37:10,603 --> 00:37:12,313
It just wasn't right for us, Will.

694
00:37:13,147 --> 00:37:17,068
-And it would've torn the family apart.
-No, I wouldn't have let that happen.

695
00:37:17,151 --> 00:37:18,778
It already was happening.

696
00:37:18,861 --> 00:37:22,490
You were putting what Richard wanted
ahead of what your mom and I wanted.

697
00:37:23,032 --> 00:37:25,743
I had asked you guys to shut it down twice
and you just kept working.

698
00:37:25,826 --> 00:37:27,870
Because that's what we agreed to.

699
00:37:28,537 --> 00:37:31,290
[sighs] Look, we found a better solution.

700
00:37:31,374 --> 00:37:32,833
Right? And Richard gets that.

701
00:37:34,335 --> 00:37:36,254
Will, I want you to be involved.

702
00:37:36,337 --> 00:37:37,213
[scoffs]

703
00:37:39,507 --> 00:37:41,968
Dad, you're leasing the land.

704
00:37:42,677 --> 00:37:44,679
You get a check. They do the work.

705
00:37:45,179 --> 00:37:47,556
There isn't anything
for me to be involved with.

706
00:37:48,432 --> 00:37:49,934
What am I gonna do, just sit and watch?

707
00:37:54,355 --> 00:37:57,775
[Richard] I gotta get to my flight,
but I'll be back in a couple days.

708
00:37:57,858 --> 00:37:59,485
Say hi to the city for me.

709
00:37:59,568 --> 00:38:00,569
Will do.

710
00:38:04,573 --> 00:38:06,158
Thanks again for today.

711
00:38:06,242 --> 00:38:07,868
I'm really glad we did this.

712
00:38:07,952 --> 00:38:10,162
They were with us. I have no doubt.

713
00:38:12,665 --> 00:38:14,709
Well, uh, stay as long as you want.

714
00:38:17,003 --> 00:38:18,421
Here's a key

715
00:38:18,504 --> 00:38:20,798
in case you need
some alone time while I'm gone.

716
00:38:20,881 --> 00:38:22,842
I know it can get crowded at the Walters'.

717
00:38:22,925 --> 00:38:24,510
I'll water your plants.

718
00:38:24,593 --> 00:38:25,428
Okay.

719
00:38:26,470 --> 00:38:27,805
-I love you.
-[Jackie] Love you.

720
00:38:27,888 --> 00:38:28,889
-Bye-bye.
-Bye.

721
00:38:30,599 --> 00:38:32,601
[gentle upbeat playing]

722
00:39:01,756 --> 00:39:02,590
Hey.

723
00:39:03,716 --> 00:39:04,675
They post 'em yet?

724
00:39:06,302 --> 00:39:07,136
Yep.

725
00:39:09,138 --> 00:39:12,433
Look, um, SATs don't mean everything.

726
00:39:13,184 --> 00:39:15,394
There's still so many places
you could apply.

727
00:39:18,230 --> 00:39:19,482
I got a 1250.

728
00:39:19,565 --> 00:39:20,691
What?

729
00:39:21,859 --> 00:39:22,902
Cole, that's incredible.

730
00:39:22,985 --> 00:39:24,779
-All right, calm down.
-Come on!

731
00:39:24,862 --> 00:39:26,197
-Come here!
-Calm down.

732
00:39:27,698 --> 00:39:29,033
I got a 1250.

733
00:39:29,116 --> 00:39:29,992
Yeah!

734
00:39:32,286 --> 00:39:34,288
[gentle music playing]

735
00:39:38,376 --> 00:39:41,045
♪ Crying eyes, broken bells ♪

736
00:39:41,128 --> 00:39:42,338
♪ Back in course… ♪

737
00:39:42,421 --> 00:39:44,799
So, what happened with Kiley last night?

738
00:39:47,218 --> 00:39:49,428
Nothing. It was her grandma.

739
00:39:49,512 --> 00:39:52,807
They were moving a sofa,
and she hurt her ankle.

740
00:39:54,016 --> 00:39:55,935
-Is she okay?
-Oh, yeah.

741
00:39:57,186 --> 00:39:59,980
-How was the rest of the party?
-It was kind of boring.

742
00:40:00,064 --> 00:40:01,524
-I didn't stay long.
-Mmm.

743
00:40:02,441 --> 00:40:04,276
-Sounds like I didn't miss much.
-No.

744
00:40:05,361 --> 00:40:06,195
But I missed you.

745
00:40:06,278 --> 00:40:10,116
♪ Your love is always waking mine ♪

746
00:40:11,033 --> 00:40:16,205
♪ I wanna break down
Where your heart gets so torn ♪

747
00:40:16,288 --> 00:40:19,291
♪ It's almost breaking mine ♪

748
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:22,503
♪ I wanna lay here ♪

749
00:40:22,586 --> 00:40:24,422
♪ Lost and bitter ♪

750
00:40:24,505 --> 00:40:28,384
♪ So long I feel like I could die ♪

751
00:40:29,593 --> 00:40:33,514
♪ I wanna tell you what my truth is ♪

752
00:40:33,597 --> 00:40:36,308
♪ But it's buried down inside ♪

753
00:40:36,851 --> 00:40:39,019
♪ Oh, I had a dream ♪

754
00:40:39,103 --> 00:40:41,522
♪ That you couldn't hear me screaming ♪

755
00:40:42,815 --> 00:40:45,067
♪ Tried to tell you everything ♪

756
00:40:45,151 --> 00:40:48,070
♪ But it wouldn't stop you leaving ♪

757
00:40:48,154 --> 00:40:51,991
♪ I wanna wake up where your love is ♪

758
00:40:52,074 --> 00:40:55,411
♪ 'Cause your love is always waking mine ♪

759
00:40:57,204 --> 00:40:59,290
♪ I wanna break down ♪

760
00:40:59,373 --> 00:41:02,209
♪ Where your heart gets so torn ♪

761
00:41:02,293 --> 00:41:05,004
♪ It's almost breaking mine ♪

762
00:41:06,380 --> 00:41:10,092
♪ I wanna lay here lost and bitter ♪

763
00:41:10,176 --> 00:41:14,138
♪ So long I feel like I could die ♪

764
